From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BDK Patches <patches@bdk.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:19:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] bdk: export the BDK C ABI from the framework

The framework hides every symbol that chrome/app/framework.exports does
not name. The BDK engine (//bdk) implements the C ABI that applications
call (packages/core/include/bdk in the BDK repository) and the
BDKApplicationBase class that a BDK application's NSApplication subclasses
(packages/core/include/bdk_mac). List every ABI function and the class in
the exports, and in framework.order, because verify_chrome_framework_order
fails the build on an exported symbol the order file does not name. The
functions go before _ChromeMain, which stays the last text symbol; the
class's data symbols go after it.

chromium:build compares the framework's exports with the headers after
every build, so a function added to the ABI without a line here fails the
build.

Used by: the BDK engine (//bdk/engine) and the Swift SDK.
---
 chrome/app/framework.exports | 119 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 chrome/app/framework.order   | 119 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 238 insertions(+)

